Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:06:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/37] tools/aurora-sep: sleep-drain-probe: trace s2idle and
 list domains left on

Add arm/report/disarm, for a suspend taken any way (lid, menu). arm
snapshots the counters and starts a tracefs instance of its own that
triggers turn on at machine_suspend begin and off at the first device
resume callback, so it holds only what ran while suspended. report counts
the whole-SoC wakes (timekeeping_freeze ends), names the interrupt or IPI
that woke the first CPU each time, and tallies interrupts, IPIs, softirqs,
timers and work items per wake.

Snapshots now also record each power domain's power-off count (debugfs
pm_genpd) and the device tree's apple,always-on labels, and the report
lists the domains the kernel may power off that stayed on through a
suspend.

